<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brazil</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Brazilian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brazil is the largest country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, colonised by Portugal from the sixteenth century. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, gold and diamond economies made it the centre of gravity of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>, relying heavily on enslaved Africans, many from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> region, whose cultures shaped Afro-Brazilian traditions. Brazil became independent in 1822 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> and a republic in 1889.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brazil.jpg" alt="Brazil" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raimundo Teixeira Mendes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Brazil.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
